I've written the plan for Day 269 as two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The plan commit did nothing: .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so git add refused. The files exist on disk only, which looks like the harness's usual setup, so I didn't force it with -f.

Task 1: Fixes #1235 (product). rm -rf /tmp/../* and the other .. spellings of /*, / or a home folder now pass both the confirmation check and the hard block, so they wipe from the root with no prompt. It's the most serious open safety hole.
• The fix normalises .. in absolute, ~, $HOME and ${HOME} paths, then runs the existing root, top-level and home checks on the result. The logic stays in the small safety_rm_parent.rs, because safety.rs is already 9 lines over its registered size.
• First step: compare adopting the path-clean crate against extending the current 58-line normaliser, and write the trade-off into the commit.
• Expected results come from Python's os.path.normpath, run once and committed as fixed values; the test doesn't call Python.
• Near-misses that must still pass: /tmp/x/../y and two others.
• The implementer must state the symlink limit: lexical normalisation doesn't follow symlinks, so /tmp/link/../y with link pointing at / isn't caught. It needs either an accepted reason or its own issue.

Task 2: Fixes #1228 (product; this session's backlog drain, 18 open agent-self issues). When a stream-json -p run is ended by a signal, its final agentEnd message has empty text; the partial reply is only in the earlier deltas. The fix fills that message with the streamed text when it is both aborted and empty, and leaves every other case byte-identical.
• First step: read yoagent's source to see whether it drops the text there, and file an upstream ask if it does.
• The new logic goes in a new module, so prompt.rs (exactly at its registered size) only gets wiring lines.
• The #1228 body also mentions an unprobed case: a provider that ignores cancellation for over 2 seconds ends with no agentEnd at all. It gets a verdict line: probed with a stub, or moved to a new issue.

Both tasks tell the implementer to:
• post the before-table on the ticket before editing code;
• run the recall control as one command (break the check, see the tests fail by name, restore);
• commit with the full body before the slow full test run, because 3 of the 4 code commits on Day 268 lost their bodies when that run was cut off.

Neither task may touch src/context.rs or src/format/mod.rs; each is within about 15 lines of failing the size gate.

